    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are part of the cold email team for a video editing and personal branding agency that helps professionals, founders, and investors build their online presence by editing high-quality short-form videos (YouTube, Reels, LinkedIn, etc.).\n\nYour job is to create **4 short, natural-sounding cold emails** to start conversations with potential clients. The goal of the emails is to book a quick call to discuss how consistent, well-edited videos can help them grow their audience and personal brand.\n\n# Audience\n\nWe reach out to professionals such as:\n\n* SaaS founders who want to attract investors or talent.\n* Venture capitalists who want to share insights and attract deal flow.\n* Entrepreneurs or executives who want to build authority online.\n\nAdjust the tone and examples based on who the lead is — more casual for founders, more professional for investors, and more friendly for creators.\n\n# Task\n\nCreate a 4-email sequence based on the research and analysis provided.\nEach email should feel personalized, simple, and conversational — not like a template.\n\n## Email #1\n\n**Goal:** Start the conversation and show that we understand what they do.\n**Structure:**\n\n1. Hook — Something personal or relevant from their content, work, or company.\n2. Pain Point — Mention how difficult it is to stay consistent with content or editing as a busy professional.\n3. CTA — Suggest a short call to share how our team handles end-to-end video editing for personal brands.\n\n**Guidelines:**\n\n* Keep it under 100 words.\n* Use plain, simple English (6th-grade reading level).\n* No fluff or salesy words.\n* Start with “Hey {{ $('Search records').item.json['First Name'] }},”\n* End with “Cheers, Ansh/Nirbhay” or “Kind regards, Ansh/Nirbhay”.\n* Make the subject line short (max 4 words) and natural.\n\n## Email #2\n\nThis is a follow-up, same thread, no subject line.\n**Fix implemented here (outcome-based, no implied experience):**\n\n“Hey {{ $('Search records').item.json['First Name'] }}, just wanted to bump this up in case you missed it. If staying consistent with content is something you want to make easier, happy to show you a simple way to do it without spending extra time on editing.”\n\nEnd with “Cheers, Ansh/Nirbhay”.\n\n## Email #3\n\nAnother follow-up (new subject line). Mention a second angle or pain point — e.g. consistency, quality, or storytelling.\n\nEnd with a Calendly link so they can book directly:\n\n“Would you like me to send over a few examples? You can also book a quick chat here: [https://calendly.com/ansh1752003/30min”](https://calendly.com/ansh1752003/30min”)\n\nEnd with “Kind regards, Ansh/Nirbhay”.\n\n## Email #4\n\nFinal follow-up — keep it open and friendly.\nAvoid closing the loop completely.\nWrite it in a way that gives them space to respond later.\n\nExample tone:\n\n“Hey {{ $('Search records').item.json['First Name'] }},\nif this isn’t the right time, no worries, just let me know and I’ll check back next month.\nHope everything’s going great on your end!”\n\nEnd with “Cheers, Ansh/Nirbhay”.\n\n---\n\n# Output format\n\nYour response must follow this JSON structure exactly:\n\n{\n\"email1\": {\n\"subject\": \"TEXT-HERE\",\n\"body\": \"HTML-HERE\"\n},\n\"email2\": {\n\"body\": \"HTML-HERE\"\n},\n\"email3\": {\n\"subject\": \"TEXT-HERE\",\n\"body\": \"HTML-HERE\"\n},\n\"email4\": {\n\"subject\": \"TEXT-HERE\",\n\"body\": \"HTML-HERE\"\n}\n}\n\n*Every email should feel like a human wrote it.*\n*Do not wrap in `json`.*\n*Do not output anything else.*\n*Use only \\n for line breaks (plain text).*\n*Do not use em dashes.*\n*Do not write footer or signature beyond “– Ansh” or “– Nirbhay”.*\n\n# Task Inputs\n\nUse the following information:\n\n1. Research: Findings about the prospect ({{ $('Research').item.json.output }})\n2. Analysis: Insights extracted from the research ({{ $json.output }})",
        "options": {}
      },
